##
    What both programs in this project are about.

    This file declares no Program, so it is shared code: whichever program the build begins at,
    this is compiled with it and its names are in reach. The two programs sit in namespaces
    below this one, and a name is read outward from where it is written — so each of them
    writes 'Star' and 'Sky' with nothing qualified.
##

namespace Observatory;

public model Star

    public string name;
    public real magnitude;

    public function Star(string called, real brightness)
        this.name = called;
        this.magnitude = brightness;
    end function

end model

public model Sky

    ##
        The same handful of stars for both programs, which is the reason they are one project
        rather than two. A magnitude runs backwards: the smaller the number, the brighter the
        star, and a negative one is brighter still.
    ##
    public shared Star[] function Brightest()
        yield
        {
            new Star("Sirius", -1.46),
            new Star("Canopus", -0.74),
            new Star("Arcturus", -0.05),
            new Star("Vega", 0.03),
            new Star("Capella", 0.08)
        };
    end function

end model
